{
  "about": "Minimized regression vectors of the issue #196 differential fuzz: one per divergence category the campaign found. Each runs in its own environment (its `did`); the Rust driver records the reference verdict into tests/goldens/differential/corpus.jsonl, and the TypeScript replay holds each to the category listed for it in tests/goldens/differential/divergences.json.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "leb128_overlong_nat_value",
      "target": "decode",
      "note": "nat 5 as the two-byte group 85 00. Reference accepts 5; the runtime refuses overlong_leb128 (intended, #103 decision 4).",
      "did": "type T0 = nat;\n",
      "expected": [
        "T0"
      ],
      "hex": "4449444c00017d8500"
    },
    {
      "name": "leb128_overlong_type_count",
      "target": "decode",
      "note": "An empty type table whose count is the two-byte group 80 00. Reference accepts; the runtime refuses in the header (intended, #103 decision 4).",
      "did": "type T0 = nat;\n",
      "expected": [
        "T0"
      ],
      "hex": "4449444c8000017d05"
    },
    {
      "name": "leb128_wide_field_id",
      "target": "decode",
      "note": "Field id 97 (\"a\") as a six-byte group e1 80 80 80 80 00: longer than a u32 field's five bytes, so the runtime reports invalid_length; the reference accepts. Same rule, non-minimal LEB128 (intended).",
      "did": "type T0 = record { a : nat };\n",
      "expected": [
        "T0"
      ],
      "hex": "4449444c016c01e180808080007d010005"
    },
    {
      "name": "empty_method_name",
      "target": "decode",
      "note": "A func reference to aaaaa-aa with an empty method name. Reference accepts; the runtime refuses invalid_length by decision (round-trip symmetry with validate and encode; candid-core's HostValue validator refuses it too).",
      "did": "type T0 = func () -> ();\n",
      "expected": [
        "T0"
      ],
      "hex": "4449444c016a000000010001010000"
    },
    {
      "name": "contract_unknown_key",
      "target": "contract",
      "note": "An unknown key on a type node. Contract::from_json refuses it (unknown field); schemaFromContract accepts it.",
      "did": "type T0 = nat;\n",
      "ops": [
        {
          "op": "set",
          "path": [
            "types",
            0,
            "extra"
          ],
          "value": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "contract_orphan_type_node",
      "target": "contract",
      "note": "A type node no declaration reaches. Contract::from_json refuses it (orphan_type_node); schemaFromContract accepts it.",
      "did": "type T0 = nat;\n",
      "ops": [
        {
          "op": "insert",
          "path": [
            "types",
            1
          ],
          "value": {
            "kind": "primitive",
            "primitive": "text"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "contract_rootless_arena",
      "target": "contract",
      "note": "A non-empty arena with no declaration and no actor. Contract::from_json refuses it (rootless_type_arena); schemaFromContract accepts it.",
      "did": "type T0 = nat;\n",
      "ops": [
        {
          "op": "set",
          "path": [
            "declarations"
          ],
          "value": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "contract_identities_edit",
      "target": "contract",
      "note": "A contract id that is not a contract id. Contract::from_json refuses it; schemaFromContract does not read identities, by design (contract.ts).",
      "did": "type T0 = nat;\n",
      "ops": [
        {
          "op": "set",
          "path": [
            "identities",
            "contract"
          ],
          "value": "x"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "contract_producer_edit",
      "target": "contract",
      "note": "A producer field of the wrong JSON type. Contract::from_json refuses it; schemaFromContract does not read producer, by design (contract.ts).",
      "did": "type T0 = nat;\n",
      "ops": [
        {
          "op": "set",
          "path": [
            "producer",
            "candid_version"
          ],
          "value": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "reference_refuses_identical_func",
      "target": "decode",
      "note": "A func reference written and read at the same type func (L) -> () with L = record { a : L }. The candid crate rewrites the uninhabited record L in the wire table to empty (TypeEnv::replace_empty) but not in the expected type, so its subtype check becomes L <: empty and fails: it refuses identical types. The runtime accepts. Reference bug.",
      "did": "type L = record { a : L };\ntype F = func (L) -> ();\n",
      "expected": [
        "F"
      ],
      "hex": "4449444c026a010100006c0161010100010100016d"
    },
    {
      "name": "reference_absorbs_identical_func_in_opt",
      "target": "decode",
      "note": "The same func reference under opt, read at its own type: the reference's failed subtype check is absorbed by the opt, so it decodes null; the runtime decodes the reference. Reference bug (same cause).",
      "did": "type L = record { a : L };\ntype F = func (L) -> ();\ntype O = opt F;\n",
      "expected": [
        "O"
      ],
      "hex": "4449444c036e016a010200006c016102010001010100016d"
    },
    {
      "name": "reference_accepts_non_subtype_func",
      "target": "decode",
      "note": "A func () -> (W) read at func () -> (E) with W = record { x : W } and E = record { y : E }: W lacks E's required field y, so the wire type is not a subtype. The reference rewrites W to empty and accepts (empty <: E); the runtime refuses type_mismatch. Reference bug (same cause, the other direction).",
      "did": "type W = record { x : W };\ntype FW = func () -> (W);\ntype E = record { y : E };\ntype FE = func () -> (E);\n",
      "expected": [
        "FE"
      ],
      "hex": "4449444c026a000101006c0178010100010100016d"
    },
    {
      "name": "reference_skips_invalid_utf8_method",
      "target": "decode",
      "note": "An extra func argument whose method name is the single byte ff (not UTF-8), skipped because no argument is expected. The reference skips it without checking (it does check a skipped text, and refuses this name when it decodes the func); the runtime refuses invalid_utf8. Reference bug.",
      "did": "type F = func () -> ();\n",
      "expected": [],
      "hex": "4449444c016a000000010001010001ff"
    },
    {
      "name": "future_type_reference_count",
      "target": "decode",
      "note": "A value of a future type (opcode -2462, no data bytes) that declares one reference, read at reserved. The reference skips it; the runtime refuses invalid_principal: reference sequences are unsupported by this codec, as documented (intended).",
      "did": "type R = reserved;\n",
      "expected": [
        "R"
      ],
      "hex": "4449444c01e26c0001000001"
    },
    {
      "name": "reference_quota_skipped_vec",
      "target": "decode",
      "note": "An extra argument of type vec null with 10,114 elements, skipped. Skipping charges the reference's decoding quota 50x, which the harness sets at 2,000,000, so the reference refuses; the runtime's element budget (1,000,000) admits it. A harness policy, not a rule of either decoder (intended).",
      "did": "type T = nat;\n",
      "expected": [],
      "hex": "4449444c016d7f0100824f"
    },
    {
      "name": "contract_declarations_absent",
      "target": "contract",
      "note": "A Contract document with its empty declarations key removed. Contract::from_json accepts it (the key defaults to empty); schemaFromContract refuses invalid_contract_document (declarations must be an array).",
      "did": "service : { m : () -> () }\n",
      "ops": [
        {
          "op": "delete",
          "path": [
            "declarations"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "reference_reads_func_from_empty_wire",
      "target": "decode",
      "note": "One argument whose wire type is empty, followed by the bytes of a func reference, read at a func type. No value has type empty, yet the reference decodes aaaaa-aa.f: it reads a reference value through its subtype relation alone, where empty <: t holds. The runtime refuses type_mismatch. Reference bug.",
      "did": "type F = func () -> ();\n",
      "expected": [
        "F"
      ],
      "hex": "4449444c00016f0101000166"
    },
    {
      "name": "reference_unsound_subtype_memo",
      "target": "decode",
      "note": "func () -> (W3) read at func () -> (E3). W7 <: E7 is false (W5 has an arm x that V lacks), and the reference refuses W7 at E7 on its own; but checking W3 <: E3 visits c : opt W5 first, assumes (W5, V), proves (W7, E7) under that assumption, retracts (W5, V) when x fails (the opt rule then accepts c), and keeps (W7, E7) in its memo, so v : W7 <: E7 is answered true. The runtime refuses type_mismatch. Reference bug (unsound coinductive memo).",
      "did": "type W5 = variant { a : W7; x : text };\ntype W7 = variant { c : W5 };\ntype W3 = variant { c : opt W5; v : W7 };\ntype FW = func () -> (W3);\ntype V = variant { a : E7 };\ntype E7 = variant { c : V };\ntype E3 = variant { c : opt V; v : E7 };\ntype FE = func () -> (E3);\n",
      "expected": [
        "FE"
      ],
      "hex": "4449444c056a000101006b02630276046e036b02610478716b0163030100010100016d"
    },
    {
      "name": "label_collision_numbered_field",
      "target": "decode",
      "note": "record { x : record { 100 : text } } where another declaration writes the same canonical record as record { d : text } (the label hash of d is 100). The field-name table attaches names to canonical nodes, so the runtime keys B's field as d; the reference (and the source) say 100. Same bytes, same id, different domain key.",
      "did": "type A = record { c : record { d : text } };\ntype B = record { x : record { 100 : text } };\n",
      "expected": [
        "B"
      ],
      "hex": "4449444c026c0178016c01647101000176"
    },
